  "reasoning_log_text": "The study extensively models predictive coding (PC) and reformulates it as Biased Competition (BC). Key findings include the successful simulation of attention effects across spatial and featural selectivity, demonstrating that the nonlinear PC/BC model outperforms the linear version by avoiding negative activations and instability. The shift from subtractive to multiplicative feedback is a major finding supporting the BC interpretation over strict PC predictions. Specific quantitative results include AMI values (Fig. 5) and response comparisons between linear/nonlinear models across varying contrast levels, which support the model's efficacy in simulating empirical data."
